<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francesco Farnese, Duke of Parma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1678">1678</a>–<a href="/years/1727">1727</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francesco Farnese was duke of Parma and Piacenza from 1694 to 1727. He kept the duchy out of the worst of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a> and arranged the marriage of his niece and stepdaughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elisabeth-farnese">Elisabeth Farnese</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-v-of-spain">Philip V of Spain</a> in 1714, through which her sons later claimed Parma. Childless, he was succeeded by his brother Antonio, the last Farnese duke.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francesco-farnese-duke-of-parma.jpg" alt="Francesco Farnese, Duke of Parma" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Ilario Spolverini / Formerly attributed to Domenico Ghislandi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Spolverini_-_Francesco_Farnese,_Duke_of_Parma_-_Galleria_Nazionale,_pair.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
